msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:214
msgid "A kernel built by the community"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:216
msgid "linux-big is BigCommunity's own kernel. Its BORE scheduler favors what you are interacting with over long background jobs, and it is compiled with Clang and link-time optimization. It installs next to the standard kernel, which stays in the boot menu as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:228
msgid "Snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:229
msgid "Go back in time from the boot menu"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:231
msgid "Timeshift saves daily snapshots of the system, and each one appears in the boot menu. If an update goes wrong, start the computer as it was before; a helper then offers to restore that state for good."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:242
msgid "Compression"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:243
msgid "Files compressed as they are written"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:245
msgid "The system partition uses Btrfs with zstd compression. Files take less room and the SSD receives fewer writes, with nothing to configure."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:255
msgid "Memory"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:256
msgid "More room in the same memory"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:258
msgid "There is no swap partition. When memory runs short, pages are first compressed inside the RAM with zram, which is far faster than writing them to disk. A swapfile on Btrfs covers overflow and hibernation."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:269
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:270
msgid "Tuned for each disk and connection"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:272
msgid "Small BigLinux packages adjust the system automatically: each disk gets a suitable I/O scheduler and the network uses the BBR congestion algorithm. They are ordinary packages you can inspect or remove."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:283
msgid "Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:284
msgid "Graphics drivers that follow the kernel"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:286
msgid "Big Driver Manager installs the graphics drivers your hardware needs. For BigCommunity kernels, NVIDIA modules come prebuilt and pinned to their kernel, so an update waits for its driver instead of leaving you without graphics."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:297
msgid "Software"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:298
msgid "More software, no extra setup"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:300
msgid "Besides the Arch and Manjaro repositories, you get BigLinux and BigCommunity repositories. The Software app can also use Flathub and the AUR, and Big Pkg Installer converts .deb and .rpm packages."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:311
msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:312
msgid "GNOME, curated and ready"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/comm-welcome/comm_welcome/insights.py:314
msgid "Big Gnome Center switches between complete desktop layouts in one click. The dock, panel, menu, glass effect, screenshots and clipboard history are BigCommunity's own extensions rather than third-party ones."
msgstr ""

